   "en": "The Gemara asks: «But isn’t the opposite taught» in another baraita, that the food rose to the top while the refuse sunk below? The Gemara answers: It is «not difficult. This» baraita, which says the refuse sinks down, is referring «to» refuse in the form of «earth,» which sinks below the lentils; «that» baraita, where it is stated that the refuse rises, speaks «of straw,» which floats on water."
